"""C3 generation under proof — specification §9.4/§16.1, story S5.3.1.

    "C3 calculations generated by a model with the context contract and validated up the
    ladder before proof, so that a model output can never reach the client repository
    without passing execution."

**What this module is.** §9.4's own `GenerationRequest` (assembled directly from the graph,
the same footing `classify.py`/`rules.py` already established for facts a formal context
contract doesn't carry), §16.1's validation ladder as a real, composable pipeline, and the
bounded regeneration loop the acceptance criteria names ("up to two regeneration attempts on
parse or compile failure with the error fed back; then the field is routed to the Exception
Desk with all attempts attached"). A successful generation writes a real `Measure` (mode
`GENERATED_PROVED`), a `MAPS_TO` edge, and a `ProvenanceRecord` carrying the full
`model_call` block §4.2 names. An exhausted or declined one writes a real `ExceptionCase` —
the first story to drive that node type, the same "declared since S1.1.1, driven for the
first time" trajectory `SemanticModel.state`/`Measure`/`Pattern` have each already taken.

**What this module is not, and why each rung is what it is.** Story S5.3.2 filled the one
gap ADR 0038 named as its own: the Transpiler now calls `gateway.generate(task_class=
TRANSPILE_C3, ...)` (`.gateway`, §5.5) — a real, provider-agnostic router in front of a real
`AnthropicModelCaller`, gated by a real, Postgres-backed eval-set policy. This module still
never fabricates a check that doesn't verify what it claims (the same discipline ADR
0036/0037/0038 already applied three times in this exact epic):

- **No DAX parser exists.** `rules.dax_sanity_check` (S5.2.1's own structural stand-in,
  balanced delimiters plus a known-function allowlist) is reused here for rung 2, unchanged
  — the same honest floor, not a new grammar (a real one is its own S2.3.1-scale effort).
- **No live Fabric dev workspace exists (E11).** Rung 3 ("compile") is a disclosed,
  unconditional pass, the identical posture `FixtureTargetAdapter.smoke_query` (S4.3.1)
  already set for a capability this platform cannot yet exercise for real.
- **No Arbiter/Proof Engine exists (E7).** Rung 4 ("proof") is a disclosed, unconditional
  pass, the identical posture `model_lifecycle.regression_status` (S4.3.3) already set for
  "nothing here can compute this verdict yet."

Because rungs 3 and 4 can never themselves fail today, only rungs 1 (schema — a hard
failure, never retried, per §16.1's own table) and 2 (parse) can actually drive a
regeneration or an escalation — which is the honest, current shape of "validated up the
ladder," not a weaker version of it dressed up to look complete. See ADR 0038 for the full
reasoning.

**Two more real, disclosed data gaps this module's own `GenerationRequest` inherits.**
`model_ctx.tables`/`.columns` are empty: no `Field→ModelTable` `MAPS_TO` edge has ever been
written by any story (the Modeller's own S4.1.1 output never populated them — a real,
separate gap this module does not attempt to fix). `charter_excerpt` names no live G1
Tolerance Charter: nothing in this codebase has ever recorded one (§4.4's charter/tolerance
mechanism is not built). Both are disclosed directly in the request document rather than
silently omitted.

**Story S5.3.3 adds real confidence calibration (`.calibration`, §16.3).** Every attempt
that declares a confidence is recorded as a real observation, win or lose; before running
the ladder, `generate_c3_field` checks whether `TRANSPILE_C3`'s own calibration has crossed
`calibration.DEFAULT_CALIBRATION_FLOOR` and, if so, runs the ladder against
`TRANSPILE_C3_SMALL_MODEL` instead — a real routing decision onto a disclosed-absent
destination (no small-model `ModelCaller` is ever registered), the identical footing
Azure OpenAI already has under `TRANSPILE_C3` itself. See `calibration.py`'s own module
docstring for why this reroute is designed to stay pinned rather than self-heal.
"""

